# debugger-workstation — Cursor rules

Authoritative file: root `AGENTS.md`.

Skeleton reverse-engineering station. No third-party binaries in git. Restore with `manifests/` + `scripts/bootstrap.ps1`. In-tree core: `mcp/debugger-router`, `mcp/bin`.

## Init (ask, then act)

1. Explore (read-only): `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `manifests/*.json`.
2. Ask: install root, scope, clone MCP?, download binaries?, client, Npcap? — `templates/INIT_QUESTIONNAIRE.md`.
3. Plan, then confirm.
4. `bootstrap.ps1` dry-run → `-Apply` → optional `-CloneMcp` → authorized `download-tools.ps1 -Apply`.

## High-risk

Drivers / Npcap / Defender / samples on the host: brief consequences and rollback, then follow intent. Do not silent-install drivers.

## MCP

Default: `debugger-router` only. Never `mcp-all` in user-global Cursor MCP. If the host already has idalib, do not add a second IDA server.
